'''Chun-Li''' is a [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that was implemented in [[Version 8.10 Update#Update 8.10.5|Version 8.10.5]] and can be obtained by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Street Fighter Collaboration Event]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 512
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Chun-Li
|name2 = Chun-Li CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Chun-Li CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
There are 2 main ways to use this unit: as a rusher with massive health AND damage or as a solid crowd controller.

Chun-Li, when paired with any meatshield, is already enough to take care of enemies such as [[Bore]] or [[Mesocosmocyclone]] with little trouble, so long as there isn't much support to get in the way.

She can be used as a second A. Bahamut in stages where there is a main threat that needs to be disposed of, trading Area Attack and speed for range and health, which usually allow her to dish out much more damage while staying at a safer distance. This is most evident against enemies such as [[Daboo of the Dead|Daboo]] or [[Sunfish Jones]].

Her fast attacks allow her to be effective against certain traitless enemies like [[Dolphina]], [[Mr. Mole]] (who only barely hinders this unit), [[Henry]] or [[Croakley]].

Due to her range, using her is not recommended against units who outrange her and attack often with strong attacks, such as [[M. Ost]] and [[H. Nah]], while her single target makes her less valuable against hordes such as the many stages that spam [[Shadow Boxer K]].

She is similar in many ways to [[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]], having similar high HP and DPS, single-target attacks at a fast rate, multi-hit, and a good chance of knocking back certain traits.

{{Job|Classification = Rusher & Crowd-Controller}}

